 515  *==============================================================================
 516  * 2. Calibration of variables
 517  *==============================================================================
 518   
 519  Parameter
 520  *==============================================================================
 521  *  2.1 Variables in GTAP DB
 522  *==============================================================================
 523  * These are the variables from GTAP DB format 6 verion used in the calibration process.
 524  * Population data is in million while all other data are expressed in millions of USD
 525   
 526   EVOS(endw,acts,reg)            Endowments at agents prices
 527   FBEP(endw,acts,reg)            Factor-based subsidies
 528   FTRV(endw,acts,reg)            Taxes - Factor Employment Tax Revenue
 529   MFRV(comm,reg,reg)             Protection MFA export subsidy equivalent
 530   OSEP(comm,reg)                 Ordinary output subsidies
 531   POP(reg)                       Population
 532   TFRV(comm,reg,reg)             Protection Ordinary Import Duty
 533   VDEP(reg)                      Capital Stock Value of Depreciation
 534   VDFP(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Dom Purchases at Agent Prices
 535   VDFB(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Dom Purchases at Mkt Prices
 536   VMFP(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imp Purchases at Agent Prices
 537   VMFB(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imp Purchases at Mkt Prices
 538   VDGP(comm,reg)                 Government Dom Purchases at Agents Prices
 539   VDGB(comm,reg)                 Government Dom Purchases at Market Prices
 540   VDPP(comm,reg)                 Private Hhold Dom Purchases at Agents Prices
 541   VDPB(comm,reg)                 Private Hhold Dom Purchases at Market Prices
 542   EVFB(endw,acts,reg)            Endowments Firms Purchases at Market Prices
 543   VIFA(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imports at Agents Prices
 544   VIFM(comm,acts,reg)            Intermed Firms Imports at Market Prices
 545   VMGP(comm,reg)                 Government Imports at Agents Prices
 546   VMGB(comm,reg)                 Government Imports at Market Prices
 547   VMSB(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Imports at Market Prices
 548   VMPP(comm,reg)                 Private Households Imports at Agents Prices
 549   VMPB(comm,reg)                 Private Households Imports at Market Prices
 550   VCIF(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Imports at World Prices
 551   VKB(reg)                       Capital Stock Value at Beginning-of-Period
 552   VST(marg,reg)                  Trade Exports Internatl Trans Mkt Prices
 553   VTMFSD(marg,comm,reg,reg)      Trade Margins Internatl Trans World Prices
 554   VXSB(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Exports at Market Prices
 555   VFOB(comm,reg,reg)             Trade Bilateral Exports at World Prices
 556   XTRV(comm,reg,reg)             Protection Ordinary Export Subsidy
 557   VDIP(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on dom. c in r at producer prices
 558   VMIP(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on imp. c in r at producer prices
 559   VDIB(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on dom. c in r at basic prices
 560   VMIB(comm,reg)                 Investment expenditure on imp. c in r at basic prices
 561   MAKES(comm,acts,reg)           Make matrix valued at suppliers prices
 562   MAKEB(comm,acts,reg)           Make matrix valued at basic prices
 563   
 564  *==============================================================================
 565  *  2.2 Variables in the aggregated model
 566  *==============================================================================
 567   CO(i,z)         Household consumption of commodity I
 568   CGO(i,z)        Public final consumption of commodity i
 569   INVO(i,z)       Final demand of commodity i for investment purposes
 570   DDO(i,z)        Demand for domestic production of commodity i
 571   DEPO(z)         Depreciation
 572   DIO(i,j,z)      Intermediate consumption of commodity i by industry j
 573   DSO(j,i,z)      Supply of commodity i by sector j to the domestic market
 574   EXO(i,z,zj)     Exports supply of commodity i from country z to country zj
 575   EXTO(i,z)       Total Export
 576   IMO(i,zj,z)     Imports of commodity m by country z from country zj
 577   RKDO(k,j,z)     Type k capital income in industry j
 578   RKDO_J(k,z)     Type k capital income
 579   KSTO(z)         Total capital stock in region z
 580   LDO2(l,j,z)     Industry j demand for labour l
 581   LDO2_J(l,z)     Demand for labour l
 582   LDO(j,z)        Industry j demand for labour l
 583   LDO_J(z)        Demand for labour l
 584   MRGNO(i,z)      Demand for commodity i as a margin
 585   POPO(z)         Population
 586   TDHO(z)         Household income taxes
 587   DTAX(f,z)       Direct taxes
 588   TICO(i,z)       Government receipts of indirect taxes on commodity i
 589   TIKO(k,j,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on capital k of industry j
 590   TIKO_J(k,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on capital k
 591   TIMO(i,zj,z)    Government receipts of indirect taxes on imports of commodity i
 592   TIPO(j,z)       Government receipts of indirect taxes on production of industry j
 593   TIWO2(l,j,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on wages and salaries of industry j
 594   TIWO2_J(l,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on wages and salaries
 595   TIWO(j,z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on wages and salaries of industry j
 596   TIWO_J(z)     Government receipts of indirect taxes on wages and salaries
 597   TIXO(i,z,zj)    Government receipts of indirect taxes on exports of commodity i
 598   tmrg(i,ij,zj,z) Rate of commodity i margin applied to import m from country zj
 599   XSO_I(i,z)      total production by commodity
 600   XSO(j,i,z)      Industry j production of commodity i
 601   XSTO(j,z)       Total aggregate output of industry j
 602   tssm(i,j,z)     Intermediate tax by source import
 603   tssd(i,j,z)     Intermediate tax by source domestic
 604   MAKE(j,i,z)     Make matrix valued at basic prices
 605   DSO_I(i,z)      Supplys of domestic production of commodity i
 606   XSO_I(i,z)      Total aggregate output of commoity i
 607   TotalCost(j,z)  Total Cost by industry
 608  ;
 609   
 610  *==============================================================================
 611  *  2.3 Loading parameters from GTAP database
 612  *==============================================================================
--- LOAD  EVOS = 13:EVOS
--- LOAD  FBEP = 40:FBEP
--- LOAD  FTRV = 41:FTRV
--- LOAD  MFRV = 46:MFRV
--- LOAD  OSEP = 43:OSEP
--- LOAD  POP = 42:POP
--- LOAD  TFRV = 45:TFRV
--- LOAD  VDEP = 31:VDEP
--- LOAD  VDFP = 11:VDFP
--- LOAD  VDFB = 9:VDFB
--- LOAD  VDGP = 20:VDGP
--- LOAD  VDGB = 18:VDGB
--- LOAD  VMFP = 12:VMFP
--- LOAD  VMFB = 10:VMFB
--- LOAD  MAKES = 16:MAKES
--- LOAD  MAKEB = 17:MAKEB
--- LOAD  VDPP = 24:VDPP
--- LOAD  VDPB = 22:VDPB
--- LOAD  EVFB = 14:EVFB
--- LOAD  VDIP = 28:VDIP
--- LOAD  VDIB = 26:VDIB
--- LOAD  VMIP = 29:VMIP
--- LOAD  VMIB = 27:VMIB
--- LOAD  VMGP = 21:VMGP
--- LOAD  VMGB = 19:VMGB
--- LOAD  VMPP = 25:VMPP
--- LOAD  VMPB = 23:VMPB
--- LOAD  VMSB = 35:VMSB
--- LOAD  VCIF = 34:VCIF
--- LOAD  VKB = 39:VKB
--- LOAD  VST = 36:VST
--- LOAD  VTMFSD = 38:VTMFSD
--- LOAD  VXSB = 32:VXSB
--- LOAD  VFOB = 33:VFOB
--- LOAD  XTRV = 44:XTRV
 616   
 617  *==============================================================================
 618  * 2.4 Mapping between variables in the model and GTAP
 619  *==============================================================================
 620  *==============================================================================
 621  * 2.4.1 Households consumption
 622  *==============================================================================
 623  * Households consumption is given by the sum of domestic purchases at
 624  * agents prices (VDPP) and private household imports at agents prices (VMPP).
 625   
 626   CO(i,z)         = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 627                         VDPP(comm,reg)+VMPP(comm,reg)};
 628   
 629   CO(i,z)$(CO(i,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 630   
 631  *==============================================================================
 632  * 2.4.2 Public final consumption
 633  *==============================================================================
 634  * Public final consumption is given by the sum of domestic purchases at
 635  * agents prices (VDGP) and public final imports at agents prices (VMGP).
 636   
 637   CGO(i,z)        = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 638                         VDGP(comm,reg)+VMGP(comm,reg)};
 639   
 640   CGO(i,z)$(CGO(i,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 641   
 642  *==============================================================================
 643  * 2.4.3 Demand for investment purposes
 644  *=============================================================================
 645  *  In the GTAP data, the accumulation account is presented in the
 646  *  production sector CGDS (Capital goods). Demand for investment purposes
 647  *  is thus given by the sum of domestic purchases at agents prices (VDIP)
 648  *  and public final imports at agents prices (VMIP) for this sector.
 649   
 650   INVO(i,z)       = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 651                        VDIP(comm,reg)+VMIP(comm,reg)};
 652   
 653   INVO(i,z)$(INVO(i,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 654   
 655  *==============================================================================
 656  * 2.4.4 Intermediate demand
 657  *==============================================================================
 658  * Intermediate consumption is given by the sum of domestic purchases at
 659  * agents prices (VDFP) and public final imports at agents prices (VMFP).
 660   
 661   DIO(i,j,z)      = SUM[(comm,acts,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 662                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 663                        VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+VMFP(comm,acts,reg)];
 664   
 665   DIO(ene,j2,z)$(DIO(ene,j2,z) lt 0.1) = sum(enee,DIO(enee,j2,z))*0.015 ;
 666   DIO(i,j,z)$(DIO(i,j,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 667   
 668  * for data balancing
 669  * DIO(i,'09_PAPERPRO','05_MNG')$(DIO(i,'09_PAPERPRO','05_MNG') lt 0.0000068505) = 0.000001 ;
 670   
 671   tssm(i,j,z)    = SUM[(comm,acts,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 672                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 673                        VMFP(comm,acts,reg)-VMFB(comm,acts,reg)];
 674   
 675   tssd(i,j,z)    = SUM[(comm,acts,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 676                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 677                        VDFP(comm,acts,reg)-VDFB(comm,acts,reg)];
 678   
 679  *==============================================================================
 680  * 2.4.5 Imports
 681  *==============================================================================
 682  * Imports are defined in GTAP at world prices (VCIF) and at market prices
 683  * (VMSB). Data on bilateral flows also include margins on imports (VTMFSD) and
 684  * import duties (TFRV). On the export side, the database includes exports at
 685  * market prices (VXSB), at world prices (VFOB) and subsidies on exports (MFRV
 686  * and XTRV).
 687  * The relationships between those variables is the following:
 688  *       VMSB = VCIF + TFRV
 689  *       VCIF = VFOB + VTMFSD
 690  *       VXSB = VFOB - MFRV - XTRV
 691  *
 692  * Imports are evaluated at world prices (VCIF) less transport margins (VTMFSD).
 693   
 694  ** Elimination of trade within a country:
 695  ** Trade within any entity that is a GTAP single-country region (or equivalent)
 696  ** is removed.
 697   VCIF(comm,z1c,z1c)        = 0;
 698   VTMFSD(marg,comm,z1c,z1c) = 0;
 699   
 700   IMO(i,zj,z)     = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 701                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 702                         VCIF(comm,regj,reg)-
 703                         SUM[marg,VTMFSD(marg,comm,regj,reg)]};
 704  *lt Strictly less than
 705   IMO(i,zj, z)$(IMO(i, zj, z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 706   IMO(i,zj,z)$sameas(zj,z) = 0 ;
 707   
 708  * IMO(i,zj,z)$(abs(IMO(i,zj,z)) < 1e-3) = 0;
 709  * IMO(i,zj,z)$sameas(zj,z) = 0 ;
 710   
 711  *==============================================================================
 712  * 2.4.6 Exports
 713  *==============================================================================
 714  *  To limit the sources of potential desequilibrium, exports are simply set
 715  *  equal to imports.
 716   
 717   EXO(i,zj,z)     = IMO(i,zj,z);
 718   EXTO(i,z)       = sum(zj, EXO(i,z,zj));
 719   
 720  * VXSB(comm,z1c,z1c)        = 0;
 721   
 722  * Alternative method bring the export value
 723  * EXO(i,zj,z)     = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 724  *                       $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 725  *                       VXSB(comm,regj,reg)};
 726  *
 727  *;
 728   
 729  * EXO(i,zj,z)$(abs(EXO(i,zj,z)) < 1e-8) = 1e-3;
 730  * EXTO(i,z)       = sum(zj, EXO(i,z,zj));
 731   
 732  *==============================================================================
 733  * 2.4.7 Margins
 734  *==============================================================================
 735  *  Transport margins are given by the variable VTMFSD
 736  * tmrg(TRP,ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 737  *                 = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[j2comm(ij,comm)
 738  *                       $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 739  *                       SUM[marg,VTMFSD(marg,comm,regj,reg)]};
 740   
 741   tmrg('20_LTRP',ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 742                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(ij,comm)
 743                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 744                         VTMFSD('otp',comm,regj,reg)};
 745   
 746   tmrg('20_LTRP',ij,zj,z)$(tmrg('20_LTRP',ij,zj,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 747   
 748   tmrg('21_WTRP',ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 749                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(ij,comm)
 750                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 751                         VTMFSD('wtp',comm,regj,reg)};
 752   
 753   tmrg('21_WTRP',ij,zj,z)$(tmrg('21_WTRP',ij,zj,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 754   
 755   tmrg('22_ATRP',ij,zj,z)$IMO(ij,zj,z)
 756                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(ij,comm)
 757                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 758                         VTMFSD('atp',comm,regj,reg)};
 759   
 760   tmrg('22_ATRP',ij,zj,z)$(tmrg('22_ATRP',ij,zj,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 761   
 762   
 763  * Supply of transport margin are given by the variable VST
 764   MRGNO(i,z)      = SUM{(marg,reg)$[i2comm(i,marg)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 765                         VST(marg,reg)};
 766   
 767   MRGNO(i,z)$(MRGNO(i,z)lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 768   
 769  *==============================================================================
 770  * 2.4.8 Import duties
 771  *==============================================================================
 772  *  Import duties are given by the variable TFRV
 773   
 774   TIMO(i,zj,z)$IMO(i,zj,z)
 775                   = SUM{(comm,regj,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 776                         $z2reg(zj,regj)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 777                         TFRV(comm,regj,reg)};
 778   
 779  *==============================================================================
 780  * 2.4.9 Taxes on exports
 781  *==============================================================================
 782  *  Taxes on exports are given by the sum of MFRV and XTRV
 783   
 784   TIXO(i,z,zj)$IMO(i,z,zj)
 785                   = SUM{(comm,reg,regj)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 786                         $z2reg(z,reg)$z2reg(zj,regj)],
 787                         MFRV(comm,reg,regj)+XTRV(comm,reg,regj)};
 788   
 789  *==============================================================================
 790  * 2.4.10 Taxes on factors of production
 791  *==============================================================================
 792  * Net taxes on factor of production are calculated as taxes (FTRV)
 793  * less subsidies (FBEP).
 794   
 795   TIWO2(l,j,z)     = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(l,endw)
 796                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 797                         FTRV(endw,acts,reg)+
 798                         FBEP(endw,acts,reg)};
 799   
 800   TIWO2_J(l,z)   = SUM(j, TIWO2(l,j,z));
 801   
 802   TIWO(j,z) = SUM(l, TIWO2(l,j,z));
 803   
 804   TIWO_J(z)   = SUM(j, TIWO(j,z));
 805   
 806   TIKO(k,j,z)     = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(k,endw)
 807                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 808                         FTRV(endw,acts,reg)+
 809                         FBEP(endw,acts,reg)};
 810   
 811   TIKO_J(k,z) = SUM(j, TIKO(k,j,z));
 812   
 813  *==============================================================================
 814  * 2.4.11 Taxes on production
 815  *==============================================================================
 816  * Taxes on production are set equal to the negative value of production
 817  * subsidies (OSEP).
 818   
 819   TIPO(j,z)       = SUM{(comm,reg)$[j2comm(j,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 820                         OSEP(comm,reg)};
 821   
 822  *==============================================================================
 823  * 2.4.12 Domestic taxes on commodities
 824  *==============================================================================
 825  * Domestic taxes on commodities are evaluated as the difference between
 826  * demand at agent prices and demand at market prices.
 827   
 828   TICO(i,z)       = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 829                        VDPP(comm,reg)-VDPB(comm,reg)
 830                       +VMPP(comm,reg)-VMPB(comm,reg)
 831                       +VDGP(comm,reg)-VDGB(comm,reg)
 832                       +VMGP(comm,reg)-VMGB(comm,reg)
 833                       +SUM[acts,VDFP(comm,acts,reg)
 834                            +VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]
 835   
 836                       -SUM[acts,VDFB(comm,acts,reg)
 837                             +VMFB(comm,acts,reg)]};
 838   
 839   
 840  *Balancing 2019
 841   
 842  TICO('04_GAS','06_PRK')   = TICO('04_GAS','06_PRK') -3.59655 -1.0;
 843  TICO('04_GAS','05_MNG')   = TICO('04_GAS','05_MNG') -2.15382 -1.0;
 844  TICO('03_OIL','05_MNG')   = TICO('03_OIL','05_MNG') -3.30004 -1.0;
 845  TICO('03_OIL','06_PRK')   = TICO('03_OIL','06_PRK') -2.13592 -1.0;
 846   
 847  *==============================================================================
 848  * 2.4.13 Direct taxes
 849  *==============================================================================
 850  * Direct taxes is given by the difference between factor payment at
 851  * market prices (EVFB) and endowment at agent prices (EVOS)
 852   
 853   TDHO(z)            = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),
 854                         SUM[endw,SUM(acts,EVFB(endw,acts,reg))
 855                         -SUM(acts,EVOS(endw, acts, reg))]};
 856   
 857   DTAX(f,z)          = SUM{(endw,reg)$[f2endw(f,endw)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 858                         SUM[acts,EVFB(endw,acts,reg)] -
 859                         SUM[acts,EVOS(endw,acts, reg)]} ;
 860   
 861  *==============================================================================
 862  * 2.4.14 Factors of production
 863  *==============================================================================
 864  * Remuneration of the production factors is evaluated at market prices,
 865  * that is before taxes (EVFB).
 866   
 867   LDO2(l,j,z)       = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(l,endw)
 868                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 869                         EVFB(endw,acts,reg)};
 870   
 871   LDO2(l,j,z)$(LDO2(l,j,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 872   LDO2_J(l,z)  = SUM(j,LDO2(l,j,z)) - DTAX(l,z);
 873   
 874   LDO(j,z) = SUM(l,LDO2(l,j,z));
 875   LDO_J(z) = SUM(j,LDO(j,z));
 876   
 877   RKDO(k,j,z)      = SUM{(endw,acts,reg)$[f2endw(k,endw)
 878                         $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 879                         EVFB(endw,acts,reg)};
 880   
 881   RKDO("cap",j,z)$(RKDO("cap",j,z) lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 882   RKDO("natr","04_GAS","01_KOR")$(RKDO("natr","04_GAS","01_KOR") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 883   RKDO("natr","04_GAS","05_MNG")$(RKDO("natr","04_GAS","05_MNG") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 884   RKDO("natr","04_GAS","06_PRK")$(RKDO("natr","04_GAS","06_PRK") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 885   RKDO("natr","05_MINING","06_PRK")$(RKDO("natr","05_MINING","06_PRK") lt 0.1) = 0.1 ;
 886   
 887  * Total capital stock at the beginning of the period
 888   KSTO(z)         = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),VKB(reg)};
 889   
 890  *==============================================================================
 891  * 2.4.15 Depreciation
 892  *==============================================================================
 893  * Depreciation is given by the variable VDEP
 894   
 895   DEPO(z)         = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),VDEP(reg)};
 896   
 897  *==============================================================================
 898  * 2.4.16 Population
 899  *==============================================================================
 900  *  Population by region
 901   POPO(z)         = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),POP(reg)};
 902   
 903  *==============================================================================
 904  * 2.4.17 Domestic demand
 905  *==============================================================================
 906  * Once again, to avoid descrepencies, domestic purchases are calculated
 907  * by substracting imports, transport margins and indirect taxes from total
 908  * domestic absorption.
 909   
 910   DDO(i,z)        = CO(i,z)+CGO(i,z)+INVO(i,z)+SUM[j,DIO(i,j,z)]-TICO(i,z)
 911                     -SUM[zj,TIMO(i,zj,z)]-SUM[zj,IMO(i,zj,z)]
 912                     -SUM[(ij,zj),tmrg(ij,i,zj,z)];
 913   
 914  *==============================================================================
 915  * 2.4.18 MAKE Matrix
 916  *==============================================================================
 917   
 918   MAKE(j,i,z) = SUM[(acts,comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)
 919                        $j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
 920                        MAKEB(comm,acts,reg)];
 921   
 922  *==============================================================================
 923  * 2.5 Equilibrate data
 924  *==============================================================================
 925  *  2.5.1 Equilibrium on the world margin market
 926  *==============================================================================
 927  *  The first step would be to equilibrate international markets. As there is a
 928  *  small difference between supply of margins and demand, we chose to adjust
 929  *  the supply side by increasing or reducing each region's production
 930  *  proportionately.
 931   
 932   MRGNO(i,z)$MRGNO(i,z)
 933                   = MRGNO(i,z)*SUM[(ij,zj,zjj),tmrg(i,ij,zj,zjj)]
 934                    /SUM[zjj,MRGNO(i,zjj)];
 935   
 936  **==============================================================================
 937  * 2.5.2 Equilibrium in each region
 938  *==============================================================================
 939  *  As exports have already been set equal to imports, the remaining differences
 940  *  would appear in the national data. Total production is first set equal to
 941  *  the sum of production for the domestic market (DSO), adjusted production
 942  *  of margins (MRGNO) and exports.
 943   
 944   DSO_I(i,z)        = DDO(i,z) ;
 945   XSO_I(i,z)        = DDO(i,z)+MRGNO(i,z)+SUM[zj,EXO(i,z,zj)-TIXO(i,z,zj)];
 946   XSO(j,i,z)        = XSO_I(i,z)*[MAKE(j,i,z)/sum(jj,MAKE(jj,i,z))];
 947   XSTO(j,z)         = SUM(i, XSO(j,i,z));
 948   EXTO(i,z)         = SUM[zj,EXO(i,z,zj)];
 949   DSO(j,i,z)        = DDO(i,z)*[MAKE(j,i,z)/sum(jj,MAKE(jj,i,z))];
 950   
 951  *  The operating surplus is the variable that was used to equilibrate the
 952  *  regional data. As all other variables (income, savings and so on) will
 953  *  be calculated based on the variables described in these steps, there
 954  *  should not be any other descrepency.
 955   
 956  * for Data Balancing in 2019 Database
 957  TIPO('04_GAS','06_PRK')       = -9.19154 -0.1;
 958  TIPO('09_PAPERPRO','05_MNG')  = -7.77282  -0.1;
 959  TIPO('11_CHEMICAL','05_MNG')  = -7.2221  -0.809803 -0.1;
 960  TIPO('03_OIL','06_PRK')       = -6.11563 -0.1;
 961  TIPO('13_IRONSTL','05_MNG')   = -5.64578 -0.1;
 962  TIPO('19_eNuclear','06_PRK')  = -4.99124 -0.1;
 963  TIPO('23_eWind','06_PRK')     = -4.99122 -0.1;
 964  TIPO('24_eSolar','06_PRK')    = -4.92509 -0.1;
 965  TIPO('19_eNuclear','05_MNG')  = -4.81788 -0.1;
 966  TIPO('19_eNuclear','17_PAO')  = -4.80275 -0.1;
 967  TIPO('26_eOther','05_MNG')    = -4.80001 -0.1;
 968  TIPO('21_eGas','05_MNG')      = -4.78731 -0.1;
 969  TIPO('19_eNuclear','14_CPA')  = -4.63479 -0.1;
 970  TIPO('21_eGas','06_PRK')      = -4.12172 -0.1;
 971  TIPO('24_eSolar','14_CPA')    = -3.06953 -0.1;
 972  TIPO('26_eOther','06_PRK')    = -2.96659 -0.1;
 973  TIPO('14_NONFERR','06_PRK')   = -2.12762 -0.1;
 974  TIPO('10_PETROLCOAL','06_PRK')= -1.82929 -0.1;
 975  TIPO('24_eSolar','05_MNG')    = -0.654131 -0.1;
 976  TIPO('22_eOil','06_PRK')      = -0.408636 -0.1;
 977  TIPO('04_GAS','01_KOR')       = -0.00115488 -0.1;
 978  TIPO('04_GAS','05_MNG')       = -0.0039926 -7.1598 -0.1;
 979  TIPO('05_MINING','06_PRK ')   = -0.0394804 -0.1;
 980   
 981  *RKDO('cap',j,z)  = XSTO(j,z)-SUM[i,DIO(i,j,z)]-SUM[l, LDO(l,j,z)+TIWO(l,j,z)]
 982  *                   -TIPO(j,z)-SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)]-RKDO('land',j,z) -RKDO('natr',j,z);
 983   
 984  RKDO('cap',j,z)  = XSTO(j,z)-SUM[i,DIO(i,j,z)]-LDO(j,z)-TIWO(j,z)
 985                     -TIPO(j,z)-SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)]-RKDO('land',j,z) -RKDO('natr',j,z);
 986   
 987   
 988  RKDO_J(k,z) = sum(j,RKDO(k,j,z)) - DTAX(k,z);
 989   
 990  TotalCost(j,z) = SUM[i,DIO(i,j,z)]
 991  *                    +SUM[l,LDO(l,j,z)+TIWO(l,j,z)]
 992                      +LDO(j,z)+TIWO(j,z)
 993                      +TIPO(j,z)
 994                      +SUM[k,TIKO(k,j,z)+RKDO(k,j,z)];
 995   
 996  *==============================================================================
 997  * 3. CES elasticities
 998  *==============================================================================
 999  * 3.1 Definition of GTAP parameters
1000  *==============================================================================
1001  PARAMETER
1002   ESUBD(comm, reg)   Elasticity of substitution between domestic product and imports
1003   ESUBM(comm, reg)   Elasticity of substitution between imports from different regions
1004   ESUBVA(acts, reg)  Elasticity of substitution between primary factors in the production of value added
1005   ELFKLE(acts, reg)  Elasticity of substitution between VA-energy sub-production
1006   
1007  *==============================================================================
1008  * 3.2 Definition in PEP w
1009  *==============================================================================
1010   sigma_M1(i,z)   Elasticity (CES - composite commodity)
1011   sigma_M2(i,z)   Elasticity (CES - composite import)
1012   sigma_VA(j,z)   Elasticity (CES - value added)
1013   sigma_KLE(j,z)  Elastcitiy (CES - KL-E)
1014   
1015  *==============================================================================
1016  * 3.3 Temporary variables
1017  *==============================================================================
1018   IM_GTAP(comm,z)  Total imports using the GTAP commodity sets
1019   Q_GTAP(comm,z)   Composite commodity using the GTAP commodity sets
1020   VA_GTAP(acts,z)  Value added using the GTAP sectors
1021   KLE_GTAP(acts,z) KLE using the GTAP sectors
1022   E_GTAP(acts,z)   E using ther GTAP sectors
1023   SH_IM(comm,i,z)  Share of each import TRAD_COM in aggregation i for region z
1024   SH_Q(comm,i,z)   Share of each composite commodity TRAD_COM in aggregation i for region z
1025   SH_VA(acts,j,z)  Share of each sector TRAD_COM in aggregation j for region z
1026   SH_KLE(acts,j,z) Share of each sector KLE in aggregation j for region z
1027  ;
1028   
1029  *==============================================================================
1030  * 3.4 Load the GTAP file which includes the parameters
1031  *==============================================================================
GDXIN   C:\Users\kimc0\GUIDE_GLOBAL_CGE\4.SAM\Input_w-t\GTAP11c_Parameters2019.gdx
--- LOAD  ESUBD = 19:ESUBD
--- LOAD  ESUBM = 20:ESUBM
--- LOAD  ESUBVA = 61:ESUBVA
--- LOAD  ELFKLE = 62:ELFKLE
1034   
1035  *==============================================================================
1036  *  3.5 sigma_M1
1037  *==============================================================================
1038  * Elasticities of substitution between domestic product and imports are
1039  * aggregated acording to the share of each commodity (QO) TRAD_COMM in total I
1040   
1041   Q_GTAP(comm,z)
1042                   = SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),
1043                     VDPP(comm,reg)+VMPP(comm,reg)+
1044                     VDGP(comm,reg)+VMGP(comm,reg)+
1045                     VDIP(comm,reg)+VMIP(comm,reg)+
1046                     SUM[acts,VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+
1047                         VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]};
1048   
1049   
1050   SH_Q(comm,i,z)$i2comm(i,comm)
1051                   = Q_GTAP(comm,z)/
1052                     SUM{commi$i2comm(i,commi),
1053                         Q_GTAP(commi,z)};
1054   
1055   sigma_M1(i,z)   = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1056                     ESUBD(comm,reg)*SH_Q(comm,i,z)};
1057   
1058  *==============================================================================
1059  *  3.6 sigma_M2
1060  *==============================================================================
1061  * Elasticities of substitution between imports from different partners are
1062  * aggregated acording to the share of total import (IMTO) TRAD_COMM in total I
1063   
1064   IM_GTAP(comm,z)
1065                   = SUM[regj,SUM{reg$z2reg(z,reg),VCIF(comm,regj,reg)}];
1066   
1067   SH_IM(comm,i,z)$i2comm(i,comm)
1068                   = IM_GTAP(comm,z)/
1069                     SUM{commi$i2comm(i,commi),
1070                         IM_GTAP(commi,z)};
1071   
1072   sigma_M2(i,z)   = SUM{(comm,reg)$[i2comm(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1073                     ESUBM(comm,reg)*SH_IM(comm,i,z)};
1074   
1075  *==============================================================================
1076  *  3.7 sigma_VA
1077  *==============================================================================
1078  * Elasticities of substitution between factors of production are aggregated
1079  * acording to the share of each sector (VA) TRAD_COMM in total I
1080   
1081   VA_GTAP(acts,z)
1082                   = SUM{endw,
1083                         SUM[reg$z2reg(z,reg),EVFB(endw,acts,reg)]};
1084   
1085   SH_VA(acts,j,z)$j2acts(j,acts)
1086                   = VA_GTAP(acts,z)/
1087                     SUM{actsj$j2acts(j,actsj),
1088                         VA_GTAP(actsj,z)};
1089   
1090   sigma_VA(j,z)   = SUM{(acts,reg)$[j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1091                     ESUBVA(acts,reg)*SH_VA(acts,j,z)};
1092   
1093  *==============================================================================
1094  *  3.8 sigma_KLE
1095  *==============================================================================
1096   KLE_GTAP(acts,z)
1097                   = SUM{endw,
1098                         SUM[reg$z2reg(z,reg),EVFB(endw,acts,reg)]} +
1099                       SUM[i,
1100                          SUM[(comm,reg)$[i2comm2(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1101                               VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]];
1102   
1103   E_GTAP(acts,z)
1104                   = SUM[i,
1105                          SUM[(comm,reg)$[i2comm2(i,comm)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1106                               VDFP(comm,acts,reg)+VMFP(comm,acts,reg)]];
1107   
1108   SH_KLE(acts,j,z)$j2acts(j,acts)
1109                   = KLE_GTAP(acts,z)/
1110                     SUM{actsj$j2acts(j,actsj),
1111                         KLE_GTAP(actsj,z)};
1112   
1113   sigma_KLE(j,z)   = SUM{(acts,reg)$[j2acts(j,acts)$z2reg(z,reg)],
1114                      ELFKLE(acts, reg)*SH_KLE(acts,j,z)};
1115   
1116  *==============================================================================
1117  * 4. Own price elasticities (Conditional)
1118  *==============================================================================
1119  PARAMETER
1120   E_Composite(j,z)      E nest susbtitution elasticies
1121   KLE_Composite(j,z)    KLE nest susbtitution elasticies
1122   elas_E(j,z)           Own price elasticities(Composite Energy)
1123   elas_elec(j,z)        Own price elasticities(electricity)
1124   elas_gas(j,z)         Own price elasticities(gas)
1125   elas_oil(j,z)         Own price elasticities(oil)
1126   elas_coal(j,z)        Own price elasticities(coal)
1127   elas_petrolcoal(j,z)  Own price elasticities(petrolcoal)
1128  ;
1129   
1130   E_Composite(j,z)   = SUM{(acts)$[j2acts(j,acts)], E_GTAP(acts,z)};
1131   KLE_Composite(j,z) = SUM{(acts)$[j2acts(j,acts)], KLE_GTAP(acts,z)};
1132   
1133   elas_E(j,z) = sigma_KLE(j,z)*(1- E_Composite(j,z)/KLE_Composite(j,z));
1134   elas_elec(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('18_ELEC',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1135   elas_gas(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('04_GAS',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1136   elas_oil(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('03_OIL',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1137   elas_coal(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('02_COAL',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1138   elas_petrolcoal(j,z) = 1.1*(1- DIO('10_PETROLCOAL',j,z)/E_Composite(j,z));
1139   
1140  *==============================================================================
1141  * Projections used in Recursive Dynamic model
1142  *==============================================================================
1143  PARAMETER
1144   ACT_POP(z,time)         Active population from 1980 to 2050 based on the PEP w aggregation
1145  * ACT_POP_GTAP8(reg,time) Active population from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1146   CAB_Foure(z,time)       Implicit CAB in Foure et al projections
1147   exogro(z,time)          Exogenous growth factor for exogenously growing variables
1148   exogro_LS(z,time)       Exogenous growth factor for exogenously growing labor supply
1149   g_GDP(z,time)           GDP growth
1150   g_KS(z,time)            Capital stock growth rate
1151   g_LS(z,time)            Active population growth rate
1152   g_POP(z,time)           Population growth rate
1153   g_SDR(z,time)           Domestic savings rate growth rate
1154   GDP(z,time)             GDP projection based on the PEP w aggregation
1155  * GDP_GTAP8(reg,time)     GDP from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1156   gdp_per_cap(z)          GDP per capita
1157   I_rate(z,time)          Investment rate - domestic savings over GDP
1158   Invest(z,time)          Investments from 1980 to 2050 based on PEP w aggregation
1159  * Invest_GTAP8(reg,time)  Investments from 1980 to 2050 based on GTAP8 aggregation
1160  * K_Stock_GTAP8(reg,time) Capital stock from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1161   K_Stock(z,time)         Capital stock from 1980 to 2050 based on the PEP w aggregation
1162   TFP(z,time)             Total factor productivity index 1980-2050 for PEP w aggregation
1163  * TFP_GTAP8(reg,time)     Total factor productivity 1980-2050 for GTAP8 aggregation
1164   S_rate(z,time)          Savings rate - domestic savings over GDP
1165   Savings(z,time)         Domestic savings from 1980 to 2050 based on PEP w aggregation
1166  * Savings_GTAP8(reg,time) Domestic savings from 1980 to 2050 based on GTAP8 aggregation
1167   sdr_fac(z,time)         Exogenous change factor for domestic savings rate
1168   TOT_POP(z,time)         Total population from 1980 to 2050 based on the PEP w aggregation
1169  * TOT_POP_GTAP8(reg,time) Total population from 1980 to 2050 based on the GTAP8 aggregation
1170   CTAX_Cal(z,time)        Carbon Tax for Baseline Scenario
1171   CTAX_CPS(z,time)        Carbon Tax for Current Policy Scenario
1172   CTAX_NZS(z,time)        Carbon Tax for Net-Zero Scenario
1173   EMPLOY(j,z)             Employment by sector 2019 (thousand)
1174   AEEI_low(z,time)        Autonomous energy efficiency improvement
1175   AEEI_high(z,time)       Autonomous energy efficiency improvement
1176   TREND(z,time)           Value to Physical quantity
1177   TREND2(z,time)          Value to Physical quantity
1178   TREND_CPS(z,time)       Value to Physical quantity
1179   TREND_NZS(z,time)       Value to Physical quantity
1180   PERMIT_Cal(z,time)      PERMIT
1181  ;
1182   
GDXIN   C:\Users\kimc0\GUIDE_GLOBAL_CGE\4.SAM\Input_w-t\Projection.gdx
--- LOAD  GDP = 1:GDP
--- LOAD  TOT_POP = 2:TOT_POP
--- LOAD  g_SDR = 3:g_SDR
--- LOAD  AEEI_low = 4:AEEI_low
--- LOAD  AEEI_high = 5:AEEI_high
--- LOAD  TREND = 6:TREND
--- LOAD  TREND2 = 7:TREND2
--- LOAD  TREND_CPS = 8:TREND_CPS
--- LOAD  TREND_NZS = 9:TREND_NZS
--- LOAD  CTAX_Cal = 10:CTAX_Cal
--- LOAD  CTAX_CPS = 11:CTAX_CPS
--- LOAD  CTAX_NZS = 12:CTAX_NZS
--- LOAD  PERMIT_Cal = 13:PERMIT_Cal
